# 13. Subquery in WHERE

This is one of the most common locations for subqueries.

Example:

```sql
SELECT employee_name, salary
FROM employees
WHERE salary >
(
    SELECT AVG(salary)
    FROM employees
);
```

The subquery generates a value used to filter rows.

---

# 14. Subquery in JOIN

A subquery can also be used to create a derived result that is joined with another table.

### Example

```sql
SELECT e.employee_name,
       d.department_id,
       d.avg_salary
FROM employees e
JOIN
(
    SELECT department_id,
           AVG(salary) AS avg_salary
    FROM employees
    GROUP BY department_id
) d
ON e.department_id = d.department_id;
```

Here:

```text
Subquery
   ↓
Department average
   ↓
JOIN
   ↓
Employees
```

