# 26. Nested Subqueries

A subquery can contain another subquery.

This is called a **nested subquery**.

### Example

```sql
SELECT employee_name, salary
FROM employees
WHERE salary >
(
    SELECT AVG(salary)
    FROM employees
    WHERE department_id IN
    (
        SELECT department_id
        FROM departments
        WHERE location = 'New York'
    )
);
```

Concept:

```text
Outer Query
    │
    ▼
Average Salary
    │
    ▼
Departments in New York
    │
    ▼
Department IDs
```

Nested subqueries should be used carefully because excessive nesting can make SQL difficult to read and maintain.

A CTE can sometimes make the logic clearer.

